.TH "BINDLE_URLDESC" "3" "@RELEASE_MONTH@" "@PACKAGE_NAME@" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
bindle_hash_del, bindle_hash_sdel - Bindle Binary Tools hash table deletion routines

.SH LIBRARY
Bindle Binaries Tools (libbindle, -lbindle)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include\fR \fB<bindle.h>\fR
.sp
.BI "int bindle_hash_del( bindle_hash_t * " bh ", const void * " key ", size_t " key_len " );"
.sp
.BI "int bindle_hash_sdel( bindle_hash_t * " bh ", const char * " key " );"
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBbindle_hash_del\fR() function modifies the hash table referenced by
\fIbh\fR by deleting the hash element specified by \fIkey\fR of \fIkey_len\fR
bytes in length.
.sp
The \fBbindle_hash_sdel\fR() function modifies the hash table referenced by
\fIbh\fR by deleting the hash element specified by NULL terminated string
referenced by \fIkey\fR.  If the hash table was not initialized with the
\fBBNDL_HKEY_STRING\fR option, and hash elements were added with binary keys
without a NULL termination, \fBbindle_hash_sdel\fR() will be unable to match
against the key.

.SH RETURN VALUES
Both \fBbindle_hash_del\fR and \fBbindle_hash_sdel\fR always return 0.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bindletools (3),
.BR bindle_hash_initialize (3),
.BR bindle_hash_get (3),
.BR bindle_hash_keys (3),
.BR bindle_hash_set (3)

.SH AUTHOR
David M. Syzdek <david@syzdek.net>

.SH ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS
\fB@PACKAGE_NAME@\fR is developed and maintained by David M. Syzdek
<david@syzdek.net>.

.\" end of man page
